      "caption": "FIG. 1 shows a schematic structure of a separator (1) of Example 1, in which a protective porous layer (2) having a single-layered structure comprising a whisker-type material (3) and an organic binder (4) is formed on a porous base material (5). FIG. 2 shows a schematic structure of a separator ( 6 ) of Example 2, in which a protective porous layer ( 7 ) having a two-layered structure comprising a whisker-type material ( 3 ), a particular-type material ( 8 ), and an organic binder ( 4 ) is formed on a porous base material ( 5 ). FIG. 1 shows the region where more of the organic binder ( 4 ) is included in the protective porous layer ( 2 ) is shaded darker, while the region where less of the organic binder is included in the protective porous layer ( 2 ) is shaded lighter. More of the organic binder is included at the first side of the protective porous layer than at the second side of the protective porous layer. When more of the organic binder is included at the first side than at the second side, the separator may be better adhered to the porous base material ( 5 ). Hence, the separator disclosed herein has good peeling resistance.",
      "kind": "figure",
      "sheet": "1",
      "url": "https://patentimages.storage.googleapis.com/20/05/14/f09e74dd66c71a/US20170346062A1-20171130-D00000.png"
    },
